---@field jobConfigs? gcp.unstable.devicerun_v1alpha.JobConfigList Required. Configs of the jobs in the session.
---@field displayName? string Optional. User-settable, human-readable name for the session. Maximum size is 63 bytes when encoded as UTF-8. If set, must match regex: `^A-Za-z0-9*$`.

---Config to control session notification.
---@class gcp.unstable.devicerun_v1alpha.SessionConfigSessionNotificationConfig
---@field pubsubTopic? gcp.unstable.devicerun_v1alpha.StringList Optional. The Pub/Sub topics to which session events are published. Format: `projects/{project}/topics/{topic}`. See https://cloud.google.com/pubsub/docs/admin#topic_and_subscription_name_restrictions

---Config to control session output file directory.
---@class gcp.unstable.devicerun_v1alpha.SessionConfigSessionOutputFileDirectoryConfig
---@field flatDirectoryStructure? boolean Optional. Whether to write output files directly under the output directory instead of nesting them under service-generated subdirectories. By default (`false`), output files are stored under `////`. When `true`, the session ID subdirectory is never appended, and the job display name subdirectory is appended only when the session has more than one job. Output files are therefore stored under: - `//` for a single-job session. - `///` for a multi-job session. Set this to `true` when the output directory is already unique per session (for example, when a CI system generates it), to avoid redundant nesting.
---@field gcsOutputDirectory? gcp.unstable.devicerun_v1alpha.GcsPath The Google Cloud Storage path of the output directory (e.g. `gs://my-bucket/output`). The bucket must exist. If the bucket is located in another project or uses fine-grained access controls, ensure the Device Run Service Agent of the project (`service-@gcp-sa-devicerun.iam.gserviceaccount.com`) is granted access to the bucket (such as `roles/storage.objectUser`).

